Most of the core logic is ported from that project — skill-root discovery,
the SKILL.md walker and frontmatter parser, the skill store with fuzzy
name resolution, the ranking algorithm, path-safe file reads, script
classification (shebang/ELF/Mach-O), the confined no-shell script
execution mechanics, prompt-injection sanitization of skill metadata, the
system-prompt injection, and the three tools
(`get_available_skills`, `read_skill_script` family).

Intentional differences from the upstream project:

- The regex risk scanner (`scanContent`) and the interactive
  "Approve skill script" confirmation gate are **not present** in this
  project. Upstream gates script execution behind a per-run content scan;
  this project relies on structural containment instead (path containment,
  no shell, no stdin, timeout, output cap). Scripts therefore run
  unattended in headless sessions rather than failing closed.
- Rewritten in TypeScript as a single-file pi extension (upstream ships a
  bundled `dist/extension.js` plus a `pi-skills` CLI).
- Tool parameters use typebox schemas; `PI_SKILLS_ROOTS`,
  `PI_SKILLS_SCRIPT_TIMEOUT_MS`, and `PI_SKILLS_DEBUG` env config is kept
  compatible with upstream.

